@ [profile] cantor-self-work-physical-update-broker/0.1

& [PurposeAndAuthority]
  + form the complete SWA-04B contract between one published representation-only SWA-04A update proposal and one later SWA-05 publication decision
  + make physical admission mutation observation acceptance rollback and quarantine causally explicit without granting any of those effects
  + this canonical is valid for design formation only until a later milestone-specific source phase lock proof review and satisfaction signature grants exact implementation authority
  - never: treat coherent formation, a profile string, a digest, a receipt, a fixture, or this formation signature as a capability to launch or mutate

& [PredecessorChain]
  + exact SWA-03 lifecycle request checkpoint selected step and attempt precede SWA-04A
  + exact current cantor-self-work-update-handoff-request/0.1 and cantor-self-work-update-handoff-proposal/0.1 precede this profile
  + the proposal must retain RepresentationOnly PreparedAwaitingPhysicalRevalidation QuarantineWithoutCleanup and its complete unresolved physical authority account
  + current Phase3A candidate-workspace admission semantics are the only eligible fresh-admission predecessor
  + historical cantor-bounded-candidate-mutation/0.1 and cantor-candidate-seal-review/0.1 are formation predecessors only and carry no current implementation authority

& [StageSet] is closed and monotonic
  + [B0_ProtocolPrepared] validates pure metadata lineage commissions capabilities receipts resources transitions and deterministic fixtures without I/O
  + [B1_HostPreflightObserved] may exist only under separate read-only process and observation authority and binds current executable protocol schema environment host path sandbox and admission facts
  + [B2_MutationTerminated] may exist only under separate candidate-mutation process authority and binds one stopped exact writer run or consequence-aware fault
  + [B3_PostStateSealed] may exist only under separate observation and evidence-root authority and binds complete immutable proposed-versus-observed evidence
  + [B4_IndependentlyReviewed] may exist only under separate reviewer authority over immutable inputs and returns non-promotional acceptance refusal quarantine or unresolved judgment
  + [B5_RollbackReobserved] may exist only under separate rollback-attempt and reobservation authority and binds verified incomplete faulted or quarantined recovery evidence
  + [HandoffToSWA05] may expose immutable accepted evidence for later consideration but grants no Git or publication capability
  = must: reject skipped reverse duplicate substituted or authority-widened stages

& [ClosedCapabilityKind]
  + [ReadObservation] permits only exact admitted read operations
  + [EvidenceRootWrite] permits only exact admitted content-addressed evidence publication
  + [CandidateMutation] permits only the admitted candidate path policy
  + [ProcessLaunch] [ProcessInterrupt] and [ProcessTerminate] are distinct
  + [SupervisorTest] and [IndependentReview] are distinct
  + [RollbackAttempt] permits only the exact admitted recovery plan
  + [Cleanup] [GitHistory] [Commit] [Push] [Provider] [SOPAuthorship] [SemanticSignature] [Activation] [Persistence] [Remote] [FPGA] [Minecraft] and [PrincipalWorkspaceMutation] remain distinct and not granted by profile 0.1
  + every StageCommission carries sorted unique granted and explicitly_not_granted sets whose union covers the entire closed enumeration and whose intersection is empty
  = must: reject missing duplicate unknown conflicting or stage-incompatible capability accounts before any stage transition

& [AuthorityCarrierBoundary]
  + decoded protocol metadata may name capability kinds commission identities digests bounds and expected producers but cannot instantiate a physical handle
  + process handles filesystem handles root custody current observation carriers reviewer contexts keys and rollback executors are separately owned runtime values admitted only by a later activation source
  + no authority-bearing runtime carrier implements Deserialize reconstruction from untrusted bytes
  + a receipt proves only that its admitted producer emitted a bounded statement under a named stage; it is not itself a transferable capability
  - never: add From TryFrom Default public constructor cloneable token global registry environment lookup or hidden handle recovery that turns metadata into authority

& [BrokerRoot] is exact pure metadata
  + [broker_uuid] [correlation_uuid] and [profile] are exact
  + [source_snapshot_uuid] and [canonical_uuid] bind this generation
  + [lifecycle_request_sha256] [checkpoint_sha256] [step_uuid] [attempt_uuid] and [objective_sha256] bind SWA-03
  + [handoff_request_sha256] [handoff_proposal_sha256] and [workspace_correlation_uuid] bind SWA-04A
  + [candidate_root_claim] [base_commit] [branch_ref] [Git_executable] [allowed_relative_paths] and [change_set_sha256] bind the intended candidate and proposal
  + [stage_plan_sha256] and [capability_account_sha256] bind the closed commission sequence
  + [unresolved_frontier] retains every activation prerequisite and downstream authority

& [StageCommission] is complete before activation
  + commission_uuid broker_uuid stage predecessor_receipt_sha256 producer_identity expected_runtime_profile and capability_account are exact
  + input digests output profile path policy resource budget timeout consequence policy and verifier program are exact
  + stage-specific root identities are explicit and pairwise disjoint where required
  + single_use_identity binds commission UUID stage broker and predecessor receipt
  + activation_signature_ref must identify a later exact signed artifact and cannot be supplied by profile 0.1 formation fixtures
  + commission_sha256 is domain-separated over the complete self-excluding canonical form

& [B0PureProtocol]
  + validates BrokerRoot complete StagePlan StageCommission CapabilityAccount StageReceipt FaultRecord and immutable evidence references
  + simulates all valid and invalid transitions with deterministic supplied metadata only
  + emits FormationValidated or a typed atomic refusal and never emits B1 through B5 receipts
  + performs no filesystem environment process clock network randomness provider model tool evidence write or other external effect
  + provider-free fixtures are synthetic protocol evidence and must say physical_contact false

& [B1ImmediatePreflight]
  + reruns current Phase3A against the exact SWA-04A request immediately before any B2 writer launch
  + requires an authenticated current receipt and byte-exact correspondence for root Git base branch policy budget allowlist request and correlation facts
  + binds current host OS executable digest version protocol schema digest environment digest response grammar sandbox policy canonical paths root separation process ownership interruption behavior and declared resource ceiling
  + proves candidate principal Git common-directory parent temp evidence and other writable-root separation without assuming schema text equals enforcement
  + target-host prevention claims require independent physical tests named by the later activation signature
  + stale saved structurally self-consistent replayed changed or unauthenticated admission refuses before B2

& [B2BoundedWriter]
  + exactly one pinned App Server child owns one ephemeral thread and one workspace-write no-network approval-never turn in the exact candidate cwd
  + writable roots are exactly those physically proved and granted by the B2 commission with no principal Git common-directory evidence-root temp credential remote or hidden writable surface
  + no retry steering resume fork dynamic approval or unbounded tool route exists
  + event count bytes command file-change tool call depth elapsed and output are checked before retention
  + command file-change MCP message reasoning plan sandbox and terminal events are strictly correlated and bounded
  + forbidden or outside-policy signals trigger interrupt and consequence accounting but do not claim prior writes were prevented
  + terminal success means only exact child termination and a bounded run record; it does not mean correct complete accepted clean or reversible state

& [PostStartConsequence]
  + before turn start a fault may report may_have_mutated false only when the writer was provably never launched
  + after turn start every success fault timeout interruption protocol violation process ambiguity or terminal mismatch reports may_have_mutated true or unknown
  + exact child interrupt termination reap and descendant account are attempted and recorded under their own capabilities
  + late output late file activity surviving or unknown descendants and unproved quiescence require quarantine
  + no automatic retry cleanup reset checkout clean delete reuse or second writer is allowed

& [B3IndependentPostState]
  + B2 child and all owned descendants are stopped and accounted before capture
  + exact Git executable observes top-level Git directory common directory HEAD full branch ref base tree index tree porcelain-v2 tracked untracked ignored submodule and relevant configuration state without mutation
  + direct filesystem inventory observes every in-scope path kind mode length content digest and existing ancestor identity with exact before-and-after stability account
  + link junction reparse mount hard-link alias alternate stream device pipe socket special unknown outside-policy index ref common-directory principal or root uncertainty refuses and quarantines
  + complete observed add modify delete mode-change and residue sets reconcile one-to-one with the complete proposal or refuse
  + immutable evidence contains upstream identities raw-event digests direct observations change records resource accounts uncertainties and nonauthority statement
  + evidence publication uses a separately admitted empty private root staging verification content-addressed final name and collision-equality rule under EvidenceRootWrite only

& [B4IndependentAcceptance]
  + reviewer inputs are immutable B3 evidence exact purpose criteria obligations and an independently fixed review program
  + reviewer identity differs from writer observer test runner rollback executor publisher semantic signer and activating principal
  + deterministic integrity lineage path repository special-file completeness test contradiction uncertainty and authority checks run before any optional model judgment and cannot be waived
  + dispositions are AcceptedForSWA05Consideration RefusedPreserve Quarantined or Unresolved
  + accepted means only that a later separately authorized publication broker may consider the exact immutable candidate evidence
  - never: accept mutable state issue Git instructions grant cleanup sign semantic authority activate a succeeding SOP or generalize beyond the exact evidence environment

& [B5RollbackAndQuarantine]
  + rollback begins only from a separately signed commission naming exact source evidence recovery operations expected prior state resource bounds and consequence policy
  + recovery operations cannot be inferred from Git availability worker suggestions or accepted status
  + after the attempt B3 direct observation grammar reruns independently and compares against the exact expected recovery state
  + dispositions are RollbackVerified RollbackIncomplete RollbackFaulted or QuarantinedWithoutCleanup
  + verified requires complete exact reobservation equality and still does not erase evidence or authorize candidate deletion reuse commit push or activation
  + absent authority irreversibility uncertainty or any mismatch preserves the candidate and evidence in quarantine for operator disposition

& [ReceiptFamily]
  + FormationValidationRecord PreflightRecord MutationRunRecord PostStateEvidenceRecord IndependentReviewRecord RollbackRecord and BrokerHandoffRecord are distinct profiles
  + each record binds broker stage commission producer predecessor input output resource consequence unresolved and self-digest identities
  + records retain the exact granted and not-granted capability account active at production
  + records cannot be substituted across stages producers brokers generations or profiles
  + machine-form decoding rejects unknown fields duplicate keys defaults noncanonical identities unsorted sets oversized values and trailing authority

& [FaultFamily]
  + classes are Profile Generation Source Predecessor Digest Lifecycle Commission Capability Replay Admission Authentication Interface Host Root Path Git Sandbox Process Protocol Event Resource Terminal Quiescence Inventory Reconciliation Evidence Publication Review Rollback Consequence Authority and Internal
  + faults are atomic and bind stage operation bounded message physical_contact may_have_mutated quarantine_required evidence_prefix and unresolved_frontier
  + first failing check in the closed validation order determines the fault class
  + a fault never manufactures a later-stage receipt or cleans uncertain physical state

& [ResourceAndSerializationBounds]
  + all text byte arrays collections events paths changes commands evidence references and unresolved entries have explicit nonzero maxima fixed by the stage plan
  + aggregate decoded metadata for B0 fixtures is at most 262144 bytes
  + path count is one through 64 and every path remains canonical relative under the exact Phase3A allowlist
  + every digest is lowercase canonical sha256 metadata and every UUID is canonical lowercase hyphenated text
  + strict JSON uses deny_unknown_fields and deterministic canonical ordering; duplicate map keys are refused by the exact decoder contract
  + physical raw output content and artifacts use bounded external evidence references rather than unbounded metadata embedding

& [ClosedValidationOrder]
  + profile generation and strict decode
  + source canonical and stage-plan identity
  + predecessor self-digests and SWA causal correspondence
  + stage lifecycle commission producer and capability account
  + replay single-use authentication and activation-signature references
  + current interface host root path Git and sandbox bindings when applicable
  + event process resource terminal consequence and quiescence accounts
  + inventory evidence and proposed-versus-observed reconciliation
  + deterministic review gates and independent disposition
  + rollback commission reobservation or quarantine
  + nonauthority unresolved frontier and downstream handoff

